- [ ] early-evaluation problem affecting module-level static if and type-level array extents
- [ ] mixed alias/const cycle diagnostics improvements
- [ ] constant binary arithmetic isn't range-checked against the destination, `u8 x = 200 + 100` is accepted.
- [x] exec coverage of the signed sign-bit-xor ordinal path.
- [ ] nominal aliases wrapping a restricted type do not propagate membership checking; `CpuBits cb = 16` gives a generic mismatch rather than a membership diagnostic
- [ ] restriction endpoints are evaluated by two different constant evaluators (module scope vs body scope); they may accept different expression forms
- [ ] int_domain::Domain is a single contiguous range; generalizing it to disjoint intervals would let match exhaustiveness use restricted domains
- [x] exec coverage of -fbounds-check / -frestricted-check failure paths.
- [ ] no runtime provides the synthetic `assert::__assert` the compiler emits for -fbounds-check / -frestricted-check, so a normal hosted link of such a program fails with an undefined symbol; only the test/differential stubs resolve it.
- [ ] llvm emits no trap for the IR `unreachable` after the check-failure `__assert` call (its generated .text ends at the call), so an assert implementation that returns falls through; em64t emits `ud2` (SIGILL). Either mark the synthetic call noreturn or force a trap on the failure path.
- [ ] LINK-STD harness coverage is narrower than its bug class: allocator-dupe plus the newer map-record and dupe-sort shapes exercise it; no freestanding trigger found for the physreg-reuse bug (u64/struct/f64 shuffle candidates all pass pre-fix)
- [ ] Re-check RIP-relative float/vector relocation coverage if isel grows packed memory operands or memory-operand FP arithmetic/conversion forms; the completed audit applies only to current isel.
- [x] compiler hash drift resolved: historical build recompiled isel, current tree changes lower, and same-content lower rebuild reproduces its outputs exactly.
- [x] Corrected differential record: earlier 48/48 and 59-program ALL-OK figures came from runs that discovered zero programs; the true figure then was 59 total, 58 ran, 1 diverged (dmatch2 on LLVM).
- [x] Differential-runner invariant enforced: make differential fails loudly on an empty corpus and reports programs that build nowhere as BROKEN instead of folding them into OK.
- [x] padded/mixed-width aggregate layouts covered by tests/differential/padded/ (u8/u16/u32/u64/f32/f64 mixes, enum payloads, by-value calls, containers, sizeof/alignof).
- [ ] inline asm: no tied `rm` spelling, so `inout .. in any` is rejected.
- [ ] inline asm: no test mode pins a sema diagnostic under an explicit non-host target (sema runs host-fixed in the harness); x86-only rejections like `esi:byte` are covered only via the LLVM-backend backstop test.
- [ ] inline asm: module-scope `%{..}` resolves same-TU globals and non-generic functions only; imported/`extern` symbols need only correct mangling (assembler relocation, no `llvm.compiler.used`).
- [ ] inline asm: native em64t lowering is gated to x86_64 (`select_registers` rejects all other arches); target-aware register/width validation in sema covers all four triples.
